1
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:11,900
Dear Uncle made excuses and skipped Qamar's wedding to Aspiran Ghias Abadi.

2
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:23,860
Held up by the Allies seizing the railway, Pouri got back on the wedding night.

3
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,600
Pouri, who had found a letter and learned of Leili's and my love,

4
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:32,260
threatened me that night that unless I gave up on Leili,

5
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,995
he would show my letter to Dear Uncle Napoleon.

6
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:38,660
If I didn't get that letter back,

7
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,355
Leili and I were doomed.

8
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,360
I was no match for Pouri,

9
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,840
so I kicked him in his sensitive parts and ran.

10
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:52,720
But the letter on which our love depended

11
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:56,080
stayed in the hands of my wounded rival.

12
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:05,860
What's wrong?

13
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:08,410
Nothing. Agha Jan says I'm a wimp.

14
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,310
Why?

15
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:14,170
He says I'm a wimp because I didn't, you know, with Leili...

16
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,030
I mean, I didn't go.

17
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,630
Didn't go where?

18
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:21,200
You know. That thing you always talk about.

19
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,500
Bravo!

20
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,065
Good for your Agha Jan!

21
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
He's come up with a good plan.

22
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,120
Pity that you...

23
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:38,120
are such a wimp.

24
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,520
Uncle Asdollah, if I...

25
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,560
If what?

26
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,020
If what?

27
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:45,020
If...

28
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:47,020
If what?

29
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,020
Get married?

30
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:50,020
No, Uncle Asdollah.

31
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,060
Then what?

32
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:54,020
Spit it out!

33
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:56,890
I... I...

34
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:00,570
What do I have to do so they don't give Leili to Pouri?

35
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:10,010
Bravo! Now you're finally talking like a grown man.

36
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:13,930
I've told you a hundred times: take her on a trip to San Francisco!

37
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:16,020
No, Uncle Asdollah, I mean...

38
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:19,060
Moment! Getting cold feet again, you wimp?

39
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:23,560
No, but how?

40
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,520
Do you have colored pencils?

41
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:30,655
Yes.

42
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:36,520
Go get them. A purple one and a nice pink one, and I'll draw you a picture.

43
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,560
Uncle Asdollah?

44
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:43,520
All right, I'll draw you one myself in charcoal and send it.

45
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,850
Excuse me.

46
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:49,345
Why are Your Highness's legs all wet?

47
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:52,060
It's water.

48
00:06:38,430 --> 00:06:40,260
Ghasem... Ghasem, come here!

49
00:06:40,310 --> 00:06:41,550
We're coming, Sir.

50
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:42,390
Flood! Help!

51
00:06:42,430 --> 00:06:43,840
What is it, Sir? What happened?

52
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:44,880
Help!

53
00:06:44,930 --> 00:06:46,920
Ghasem, run! Run and get a bucket! Run!

54
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:48,760
Yes, Sir, right away!

55
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:49,970
Run!

56
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:54,060
Flood... Help... Come help!

57
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,975
Where do you think you're going? Go to bed, go!

58
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:01,020
What is it, Mash Ghasem?

59
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:04,020
Looks like the English attacked, God blind their crossed eyes!

60
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,000
Sir, take this!

61
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,020
Empty it!

62
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:09,195
You have to empty the bucket!

63
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:11,505
Come back quickly!

64
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:13,260
Ghasem, hurry!

65
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:14,990
Yes, Sir, yes.

66
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,200
Run! What are you waiting for?

67
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,130
What's up, Mash Ghasem?

68
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:18,020
What's this water?

69
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,020
Why lie? Sir says it's the English.

70
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:23,720
But we don't think the English, who've barely caught their breath,

71
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:26,020
would come and flood Sir's house.

72
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:28,020
Brother, what's going on?

73
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:32,020
Brother, why are you standing there? Go empty the bucket!

74
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,520
Mash Ghasem? Mash Ghasem, what happened?

75
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:37,760
Lad, you've got some nerve showing your face around here!

76
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:41,810
Master Pouri's in a bad way. If the Colonel catches you, he'll tear you to bits!

77
00:07:42,490 --> 00:07:44,160
Is he really that angry?

78
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:48,580
Yes, lad, run and hide! Kicking a man in his honor is no joke.

79
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:52,185
You kicked him so hard his breath and his honor got all tangled up!

80
00:07:52,290 --> 00:07:53,540
Go on, run!

81
00:07:53,590 --> 00:07:55,660
Come on!

82
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:56,660
Hurry up!

83
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:58,440
Empty the buckets faster!

84
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:00,450
Take them away, not to me!

85
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:02,760
Where's the drain hole of this pool?

86
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,500
In this flood, you're looking for the drain?

87
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,350
Hurry up, man!

88
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:09,780
What are you waiting for?

89
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:11,150
Good God!

90
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,500
Is this any way to fight a war?

91
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:15,550
Take it and come down!

92
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,580
Hurry, Ghasem!

93
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:18,900
Yes, Sir. Come quickly!

94
00:08:18,949 --> 00:08:20,020
Come quickly!

95
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:20,840
Mash Ghasem!

96
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:22,430
A sack! Hurry!

97
00:08:22,470 --> 00:08:24,920
A sack for what, Colonel?

98
00:08:24,970 --> 00:08:29,040
I think someone pulled the rag out of the drain hole.

99
00:08:29,090 --> 00:08:32,460
What shameless lowlife did this?

100
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:35,780
What a childish question!

101
00:08:36,410 --> 00:08:41,410
I know the strategy of the English,

102
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:45,820
because I've fought them many times.

103
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,060
Like in the battle of Kazerun:

104
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:52,100
one night at midnight, they let the water loose under our tents,

105
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:54,535
and two hours later, they attacked.

106
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:56,560
God wipe them out!

107
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,500
They make Shemr look like a saint!

108
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:59,645
Oh, God!

109
00:08:59,850 --> 00:09:03,000
Remember, Sir, what a flood they let loose under us?

110
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:05,840
Mash Ghasem, this is a kind of Shemr trick too.

111
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:08,480
Shemr cut off the water; the English let it loose.

112
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,860
Next to them, Shemr was a saint!

113
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:13,020
Thank God we and Sir were first-class swimmers,

114
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:16,060
or else we and Sir would both have drowned by now.

115
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:19,520
Quick, Ghasem, take this bucket and empty it!

116
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:22,320
Yes, Sir. You fill it up till we get back.

117
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:23,440
Heave-ho!

118
00:09:23,490 --> 00:09:25,500
Somebody come take this!

119
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:29,860
Here, take this bucket and go! Hurry!

120
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:34,640
Where on earth is this drain hole?

121
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,100
The English must have stolen it.

122
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:41,880
Brother, the English rolled into Tehran with cannons, tanks and planes,

123
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:44,280
and then, just to do you harm,

124
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,340
they come and mess with your drain hole?

125
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,220
What kind of talk is that?

126
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:54,100
Brother, don't you teach me the secrets of English politics!

127
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:56,700
The English are obsessed with me and my family!

128
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:59,900
Heaven forbid, Sir! Who are those English dogs to fall for you?

129
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:03,300
With those crossed eyes of theirs, how could they fall for anyone?

130
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:08,700
We had a fellow townsman who said, pardon me, the English aren't even real men.

131
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:13,100
Stop talking rubbish! You talk too much. I didn't ask for your help.

132
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:15,940
Instead of this nonsense, go to the coffeehouse

133
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:19,100
and find that shoeshine boy. Bring him here.

134
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:20,300
I need him.

135
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:25,260
He might have seen which bastard came and opened the pool drain.

136
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,389
Run!

137
00:10:26,429 --> 00:10:27,229
Yes, Sir.

138
00:10:27,269 --> 00:10:29,900
He sits by the garden gate from morning till night.

139
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:33,940
He must have seen which bastard foreigner came and opened the drain.

140
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,060
The shoeshine boy wasn't there tonight.

141
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,600
Just do what I tell you! Get lost!

142
00:10:38,650 --> 00:10:39,810
Yes, Sir.

143
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:42,190
Bucket!

144
00:10:45,790 --> 00:10:46,680
Colonel!

145
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:47,440
Colonel, take this and go!

146
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,460
Why are you just standing there?

147
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,230
Give us a hand!

148
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:51,440
Brother, Brother, Brother!

149
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:54,440
See? See? It was the drain hole!

150
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,440
See? I plugged it.

151
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:59,440
No matter how often I say it's the English,

152
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:02,440
he keeps saying it's the drain hole. Unbelievable!

153
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,430
I swear to God, it was the drain hole!

154
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,480
Nobody ever listens!

155
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:12,160
The day after I kicked Pouri in his sensitive parts,

156
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:17,520
fearing Uncle Colonel, who was out to kill me, they exiled me to Dezashib.

157
00:11:18,490 --> 00:11:20,620
During my exile, I heard nothing at all.

158
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:23,160
I only heard Pouri had surgery in the hospital,

159
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:28,160
and they had removed one of his pair, which had taken a hard blow.

160
00:11:29,310 --> 00:11:33,560
Three weeks later, at a party welcoming newlyweds Qamar and Aspiran Ghias Abadi,

161
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:37,600
thrown by Agha Jan, I was forgiven.

162
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:40,780
Shazdeh Asdollah Mirza came to Dezashib to fetch me

163
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:43,980
and on the way filled me in on the events

164
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:47,100
I had missed in my twenty-one days of exile.

165
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:53,020
Uncle Asdollah, what do you think will happen to Pouri now?

166
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:58,300
Well, his body will lose its balance.

167
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,500
Why?

168
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:02,460
Well, when they take one side out,

169
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,740
one side of the body is lighter,

170
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:06,655
and the other side heavier.

171
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:09,360
I'm very worried about him.

172
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,360
Moment!

173
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,140
Really, Moment!

174
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,140
Why are you worried?

175
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,420
That horse-faced wretch should worry,

176
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:19,180
now that he's been stripped of San Francisco!

177
00:12:19,542 --> 00:12:23,460
You mean he can never go to San Francisco again?

178
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:26,600
The old healers and the doctors disagree.

179
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:28,500
The healers believe

180
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,060
he can't.

181
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:33,180
The doctors say maybe he can.

182
00:12:34,180 --> 00:12:36,835
Can Pouri get married now?

183
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:40,060
Not right away, but maybe in a while.

184
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:44,100
And even then, as Sardar Maharat-Khan says, "his nature very depressed, hey!"

185
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:48,070
And as for Leili,

186
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:51,460
don't worry, she's fine.

187
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:56,620
Do you think Agha Jan's party tonight will get rowdy?

188
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:57,620
Definitely.

189
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:00,120
Dustali Khan and Aziz-Saltaneh

190
00:13:00,262 --> 00:13:03,307
have just found out that Aspiran Ghias Abadi,

191
00:13:03,422 --> 00:13:05,620
who claimed his honor was shot off at the root

192
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:08,620
in the Lorestan forest, was lying from the root up.

193
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:09,620
From the root?

194
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:12,252
This Aspiran, who claimed he owned nothing in the world,

195
00:13:12,302 --> 00:13:14,620
turns out to be quite a rich man.

196
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:16,620
Really, Uncle Asdollah?

197
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,145
Why should I lie?

198
00:13:18,382 --> 00:13:19,997
The grave is this close!

199
00:13:20,482 --> 00:13:22,162
What a crook!

200
00:13:22,402 --> 00:13:25,057
No, he's not such a crook, poor guy.

201
00:13:26,622 --> 00:13:29,082
From the look of things...

202
00:13:29,262 --> 00:13:31,527
your Agha Jan has a hand in it.

203
00:13:31,722 --> 00:13:32,650
And Qamar?

204
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:35,060
Qamar? She's on cloud nine.

205
00:13:36,142 --> 00:13:39,317
Her husband's rich, and she wanted a baby and has one.

206
00:13:39,422 --> 00:13:42,792
I loved the trick the Aspiran played on them.

207
00:13:43,622 --> 00:13:45,130
He was to take money, marry Qamar,

208
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:46,460
and divorce her days later.

209
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:49,092
But now he's dug in so firmly

210
00:13:49,142 --> 00:13:52,832
that he's tried ten times to throw Dustali out of the house.

211
00:13:52,882 --> 00:13:55,572
And Qamar's so smitten that, for San Francisco,

212
00:13:55,622 --> 00:13:57,887
the girl would even give up her mother.

213
00:13:58,422 --> 00:14:02,112
So it's a real mess. And what about Dustali Khan?

214
00:14:02,162 --> 00:14:05,322
That donkey Dustali? He's about to have a stroke.

215
00:14:05,882 --> 00:14:09,572
Since the Aspiran, bald head and all, has stolen Qamar's heart,

216
00:14:09,622 --> 00:14:12,472
Dustali's afraid Qamar's estates and inheritance

217
00:14:12,522 --> 00:14:15,252
will slip out of his grasp.

218
00:14:15,302 --> 00:14:22,192
Funniest is the Aspiran's sister Akhtar, who lives at Dustali's and has him panting.

219
00:14:22,242 --> 00:14:26,500
This Akhtar has a street-tough boyfriend named Asghar Diesel.

220
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:28,132
Shir-Ali the butcher, part two.

221
00:14:28,182 --> 00:14:30,312
She's brought her boyfriend to Dustali's too?

222
00:14:30,362 --> 00:14:34,500
No, but every other night he shows up blind drunk, and if Dustali dares

223
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:38,490
not to open the door for him, he rips it off its hinges.

224
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:41,500
Uncle Asdollah, you seem to be enjoying all this.

225
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:44,500
Yes, I've never been happier in my life.

226
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:47,975
Let their noses get rubbed in the dirt a little.

227
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:52,500
This aristocratic family, grandsons of Palang-os-Saltaneh and Babr-od-Dowleh,

228
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:55,500
who thought they were too good for their own shadows,

229
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:59,560
are now drinking buddies with Asghar Diesel and Aspiran Ghias Abadi.

230
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,032
You mean they're all coming to our house tonight?

231
00:15:02,082 --> 00:15:03,242
Yes.

232
00:15:03,502 --> 00:15:07,912
In fact, I think your Agha Jan is the one running tonight's show.

233
00:15:07,962 --> 00:15:12,042
In short, your Agha Jan isn't one to forget Pouri's insults so soon.

234
00:15:12,102 --> 00:15:15,172
Uncle Asdollah, can't you keep Asghar Diesel away tonight?

235
00:15:15,222 --> 00:15:17,312
Moment, moment!

236
00:15:17,362 --> 00:15:22,502
Actually, I specially told the Aspiran's sister to bring Mr. Asghar along.

237
00:15:22,582 --> 00:15:24,072
You know, my boy,

238
00:15:24,122 --> 00:15:27,262
this Dustali owes me much more than this.

239
00:15:27,302 --> 00:15:31,162
If I tormented him till Judgment Day, he'd still have it coming.

240
00:15:31,562 --> 00:15:35,962
Tonight's party would be no fun without Asghar Diesel.

241
00:15:39,542 --> 00:15:43,612
Now, first you go to your Uncle Colonel and kiss his hand.

242
00:15:43,662 --> 00:15:47,192
Then he'll surely tell you to go to your Dear Uncle Napoleon

243
00:15:47,242 --> 00:15:49,117
and pay your respects. Go.

244
00:15:49,642 --> 00:15:53,642
Then your Dear Uncle Napoleon will order you to go tomorrow

245
00:15:54,082 --> 00:15:57,062
to the hospital to visit Pouri and apologize.

246
00:15:57,562 --> 00:15:58,982
Go there too.

247
00:15:59,542 --> 00:16:00,767
And after that...

248
00:16:01,282 --> 00:16:03,547
Well, go on down now. Go.

249
00:16:07,322 --> 00:16:09,240
Saeid, where's your Agha Jan?

250
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:11,090
I think he's in the hall.

251
00:16:12,982 --> 00:16:14,980
Dustali, I hear you're being thrown out.

252
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,375
Asdollah!

253
00:16:18,622 --> 00:16:19,940
Sir, what sort of party is this?

254
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:24,180
I just heard that trashy woman invited that lumbering ogre too!

255
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,480
What would you have me do?

256
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,100
You shouldn't let these thugs into the house!

257
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:30,980
Your son-in-law's sister is bringing her friend tonight.

258
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:33,820
Is it right for me to shut the door on your relatives?

259
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:36,260
Well, if I invited every Tom, Dick and Harry to your house,

260
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:37,260
would you like it?

261
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,340
Most welcome.

262
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:39,820
The Prophet said:

263
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,460
"The noblest of you before God is the most pious."

264
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,160
Very well.

265
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:43,880
Very well.

266
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:46,620
Then I'll bring one of those "most pious" over here

267
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,015
for you.

268
00:16:48,662 --> 00:16:50,200
If Asghar Diesel can come,

269
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,895
why shouldn't I invite a guest, Sir?

270
00:16:54,802 --> 00:16:55,900
Moment!

271
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:57,295
Dustali!

272
00:16:58,240 --> 00:16:59,040
Is it true?

273
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:00,175
What?

274
00:17:00,422 --> 00:17:01,320
The Aspiran.

275
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,860
Get lost, you clown!

276
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:06,595
I heard the Aspiran wants to throw you out of the house.

277
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:07,930
God forgive me!

278
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:11,980
Well, the weather's lovely right now. You can sleep in the street.

279
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:17,610
Who's he gone to invite?

280
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,130
Honestly, what can I say?

281
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,610
That lowlife is capable of anything.

282
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,130
We'll have to wait and see

283
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:24,370
how he plans to get even.

284
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,730
Get even for what?

285
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:27,060
Moment!

286
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:29,810
Seems you haven't figured out why there's a party tonight.

287
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:32,850
Isn't it for Qamar and the Aspiran's wedding?

288
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:36,460
Is your Agha Jan so smitten with Aspiran Ghias Abadi's curly locks

289
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:39,090
that he'd throw him such a lavish party?

290
00:17:39,802 --> 00:17:41,940
Even your Dear Uncle, the head of the family,

291
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:45,560
and none of the relatives threw Qamar a welcome party.

292
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,100
But your Agha Jan does. Why?

293
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:50,720
Why is your Agha Jan at odds with your Dear Uncle?

294
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,280
Do you know that?

295
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:56,060
Dear Uncle always rubs it in that Agha Jan isn't from an aristocratic family.

296
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:57,140
Bravo!

297
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,640
Now your Agha Jan wants to parade Aspiran Ghias Abadi,

298
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:03,580
son of a sheep's-head cook and brother of Akhtar the godless dancer, before everyone.

299
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:06,140
He tried it at Qamar's wedding too, but it didn't work.

300
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:07,520
But now

301
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:10,860
All the relatives know Qamar has married Aspiran Ghias Abadi,

302
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:15,560
but tonight, besides the relatives, some prominent people are invited too,

303
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:18,260
like Mr. Salar, one of the city's big shots.

304
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:22,300
By inviting Mr. Salar, your Agha Jan kills two birds with one stone.

305
00:18:23,742 --> 00:18:26,722
What is it, sir? You look all flustered.

306
00:18:30,112 --> 00:18:34,380
First, he humiliates Dear Uncle, Dustali and his family.

307
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:37,200
Second, he scares Dear Uncle to death.

308
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:40,440
This Mr. Salar is known to be a lackey of the English.

309
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:44,380
So there could be a fight between Agha Jan and Dear Uncle?

310
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:46,555
That's exactly what worries me.

311
00:18:46,672 --> 00:18:48,160
If I didn't feel sorry for you,

312
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:51,140
I'd go straight to your Agha Jan's side and give them hell.

313
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,940
Well, well, Mr. Aspiran!

314
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:54,580
Hello, Doctor.

315
00:18:54,620 --> 00:18:56,280
Hello! Look what a celebration!

316
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:57,880
You honor me.

317
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,362
Hello, Lady Aziz.

318
00:18:59,412 --> 00:19:00,897
Please, come in.

319
00:19:01,672 --> 00:19:04,020
Well, well, hello, Mr. Aspiran!

320
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,870
How's the groom?

321
00:19:06,372 --> 00:19:07,380
At your service.

322
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:09,160
How are you, Your Highness?

323
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:09,960
Doing well?

324
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,920
Just today I was telling Qamar

325
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,420
we miss Your Highness.

326
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:18,980
We must ask you to honor us one evening.

327
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:21,340
You're too kind. Where's your mother? And dear Miss Akhtar?

328
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:24,500
She's coming. She was waiting for Akhtar so they'd come together.

329
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:27,860
Well, well, what a pretty lady!

330
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:29,700
What a lovely dress, madam!

331
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,580
Mother dear made it for me.

332
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:35,900
Bless her, Lady Aziz has a hundred talents in every finger.

333
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:39,140
No, Uncle Asdollah, my Aziz didn't make it.

334
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:40,340
Mother dear made it.

335
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,820
She means my mother.

336
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:43,500
Don't be offended, Lady Aziz.

337
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:45,100
It's all the same, isn't it?

338
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,140
Well, you little rascal,

339
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:49,620
your belly's starting to show.

340
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:52,100
Did you finally knit a red sweater for your baby?

341
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:53,860
Only the sleeves are left.

342
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:55,100
Well, well! Welcome!

343
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:57,210
Please, come in.

344
00:19:57,472 --> 00:20:00,460
Finish the sleeves too, so that for your darling Aspiran...

345
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,220
Mr. Aspiran, it's cooler in the other room.

346
00:20:03,430 --> 00:20:05,680
Come... come.

347
00:20:05,732 --> 00:20:07,382
And then knit me a scarf

348
00:20:07,432 --> 00:20:08,530
too.

349
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,540
Please.

350
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:14,540
The bride and groom have arrived and gone into the cool room.

351
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:16,540
Hey, come here, let me see.

352
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,540
What's this?

353
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,540
Sour cherry syrup, sir.

354
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:22,540
Tell Mash Ghasem to bring me some of that special drink.

355
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:24,540
Haven't you heard?

356
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:25,540
What?

357
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:30,540
They arrested Mash Ghasem an hour ago and took him to the police station.

358
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:32,540
The police station?

359
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,540
What did he do?

360
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,540
Sir, you didn't hear it from us.

361
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:38,540
Sir said nobody should know.

362
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:45,540
This evening Mash Ghasem dropped a brick from the roof on an Englishman's head.

363
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:46,540
Really? You're joking!

364
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:52,580
No, sir, it's the truth. The Englishman's head is all bloody, yes.

365
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:58,580
And Sir went after them to the police station.

366
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:01,580
Moment... now it makes sense.

367
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,422
Me no want this! You broke!

368
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:08,272
Ow, ow, ow!

369
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:14,242
Please forgive him this time, let it pass.

370
00:21:14,292 --> 00:21:17,077
I'll punish him myself, officer.

371
00:21:17,432 --> 00:21:22,540
Of course it was a mistake. It wasn't on purpose.

372
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:24,530
With all respect, what is you saying?

373
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,780
How it not on purpose, sir?

374
00:21:27,272 --> 00:21:29,540
Me minding own business, walking down alley,

375
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:33,540
shouting "Fish! Fish! Fresh fish!"

376
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:38,200
"Fresh fish!" when suddenly a brick come from sky, hit me, broke my head.

377
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:41,200
Say brick slip from his hand by accident and hit my head,

378
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:43,480
what about all that filthy cursing my mother?

379
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:48,100
You tell me, those curses on my honor also just slip out his mouth?

380
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,340
You took money and agreed to drop it.

381
00:21:50,380 --> 00:21:53,680
If Sir wants to punish his own servant, it's none of your business.

382
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:54,980
Go on, be on your way.

383
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:56,980
I listen to you, officer.

384
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:58,980
All right, I'm going.

385
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:01,020
No, this not justice!

386
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:05,062
Me shameless if I not break his head!

387
00:22:05,112 --> 00:22:06,207
Well.

388
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:10,980
You stupid jackass!

389
00:22:11,020 --> 00:22:13,980
When will you ever learn, Ghasem?

390
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:14,980
Sir...

391
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:16,980
Whatever you get your hands on,

392
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:18,980
you throw at people's heads? Sir...

393
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:19,980
Yes, you idiot!

394
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,980
Sir, say whatever you like,

395
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:23,980
but we still stand by what we said.

396
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:26,980
If you don't shut up, I'll strangle you with my own hands!

397
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:30,400
That shameless man, if he isn't English himself,

398
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:32,185
he's their spy, Sir!

399
00:22:33,372 --> 00:22:34,362
I didn't do anything.

400
00:22:34,412 --> 00:22:35,520
Sir...

401
00:22:38,092 --> 00:22:38,892
Sir...

402
00:22:38,932 --> 00:22:41,820
Sir, we've been in this neighborhood thirty solid years.

403
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:45,295
How come we never saw that blasted fellow before?

404
00:22:45,452 --> 00:22:48,120
After thirty years, can't we spot an Englishman?

405
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:50,420
Ghasem, that's enough! Shut up!

406
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:52,480
We'll shut up, Sir.

407
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,660
But that poor shoeshine boy,

408
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,900
on Judgment Day, his innocent blood will be on your hands!

409
00:22:57,940 --> 00:23:03,680
That poor wretch is waiting for you to avenge his blood on the English.

410
00:23:10,292 --> 00:23:10,980
You again?

411
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:11,740
Evening, officer.

412
00:23:11,780 --> 00:23:13,915
Hello. Sit down, sit down.

413
00:23:20,270 --> 00:23:23,575
Shazdeh, we've got to get this Asghar Diesel drunk.

414
00:23:27,950 --> 00:23:30,085
At first I didn't look closely.

415
00:23:32,690 --> 00:23:34,980
Good evening. Your humble servant.

416
00:23:35,030 --> 00:23:37,580
Bless you. Have some sweets.

417
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:40,580
Bless you. We're forever in your debt, sir.

418
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,420
Thank you.

419
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:42,800
You're too kind.

420
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:44,120
What would you like? Tea?

421
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:46,940
Bless you, I've had everything.

422
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,310
Thank you very much, you're very kind.

423
00:23:50,192 --> 00:23:50,840
Don't be shy.

424
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:53,122
There's wine and beer too, you know.

425
00:23:53,172 --> 00:23:54,620
Well, since you insist,

426
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:57,000
if there's a drop of raisin arak,

427
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,000
and if not, no matter,

428
00:23:59,040 --> 00:24:01,760
a nice cold beer would do.

429
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:04,360
Doctor, our Asghar here

430
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:06,300
is a little shy.

431
00:24:07,592 --> 00:24:09,000
Some of these sweets.

432
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:12,740
Man, we don't eat that stuff.

433
00:24:14,892 --> 00:24:15,942
Go on, eat.

434
00:24:15,992 --> 00:24:18,452
Dear, it'll help your milk come in.

435
00:24:18,670 --> 00:24:20,362
I'll get a drink. A special drink.

436
00:24:20,412 --> 00:24:21,897
Here you are.

437
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,960
Eat, dear.

438
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
It won't kill you.

439
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:33,960
Tonight Mr. Asghar

440
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,850
is going to drink till he's drunk.

441
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:37,960
No, drink!

442
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,650
Bless you. Thanks for your kindness.

443
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:42,380
Moment, moment!

444
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:47,340
Our Asghar here is a bit shy.

445
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,800
Well, drink up!

446
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:52,790
Don't refuse him.

447
00:24:52,840 --> 00:24:54,455
Bless you, Shazdeh.

448
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:58,630
Leave the honored guests to me.

449
00:24:58,680 --> 00:24:59,930
All right.

450
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:01,150
Well, Asghar, my friend,

451
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,590
to your health!

452
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:03,735
Bottoms up!

453
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,755
Saeid, Saeid!

454
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Nobody downs even a lemonade as easily as you did that.

455
00:25:19,180 --> 00:25:20,665
Enjoy!

456
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:30,010
Don't you worry about the baby.

457
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:34,599
I'll swaddle it and change it myself until you learn.

458
00:25:34,639 --> 00:25:37,800
It's not hard. You just have to pay attention.

459
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:40,030
It's nothing difficult, my girl.

460
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,410
My sweetheart.

461
00:25:41,460 --> 00:25:44,000
Oh, it's you? Bless you.

462
00:25:44,060 --> 00:25:45,600
This wine is heavenly.

463
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:49,180
Oh, you devil! God keep you, Shazdeh!

464
00:25:49,220 --> 00:25:51,095
Me, drink?

465
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:53,440
On a night like this?

466
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:55,850
Bless you, you've married off such a fine young man.

467
00:25:55,900 --> 00:25:57,270
At your service. Please.

468
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:59,420
What a sweet boy this Aspiran is.

469
00:25:59,470 --> 00:26:00,250
Please.

470
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:02,000
Tonight is a night for love.

471
00:26:03,460 --> 00:26:05,205
Please.

472
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,400
Well, well.

473
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:13,140
You're getting nicely merry.

474
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,460
What are you up to, you devil? Huh?

475
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:19,530
Have some sherbet.

476
00:26:19,580 --> 00:26:22,000
Please.

477
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Go, go, go.

478
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:42,840
Cheers!

479
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:44,980
Why are you sitting there idle?

480
00:26:50,140 --> 00:26:53,315
Let's drink to our honored host!

481
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:05,060
Bring them to the dining room.

482
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:06,715
Wait. All right.

483
00:27:07,280 --> 00:27:10,380
Mr. Salar, you've truly delighted us by coming.

484
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:14,800
Mr. Ghias Abadi, our son-in-law, is a high-ranking police officer.

485
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:16,065
At your service.

486
00:27:16,300 --> 00:27:18,720
Very pleased to meet you. Congratulations.

487
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:23,100
Mr. Ghias Abadi, which branch of the police are you in?

488
00:27:23,140 --> 00:27:26,280
Criminal division, sir.

489
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:29,720
Who do you work with? I mean, who's your boss?

490
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:33,640
Well, sir, Nayeb Teymoor-Khan.

491
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:35,240
Which Teymoor-Khan?

492
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,280
Wasn't he head of the Khorasan police at one time?

493
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:39,820
Ten or fifteen years ago.

494
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:42,540
No, sir, no.

495
00:27:42,580 --> 00:27:46,020
He was never anybody's chief.

496
00:27:46,060 --> 00:27:48,700
He was supposed to come tonight too.

497
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:51,100
I don't know why he's late.

498
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:55,280
Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama is here too.

499
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,520
Why so late, Doctor?

500
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:59,110
Good evening.

501
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:00,580
Very, very pleased.

502
00:28:00,620 --> 00:28:02,580
Bless you, sir.

503
00:28:02,620 --> 00:28:03,600
How are you?

504
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,040
Please.

505
00:28:05,080 --> 00:28:08,580
Well, well! Hello, Doctor!

506
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,580
How are you?

507
00:28:10,620 --> 00:28:12,580
We've been waiting for you a long time.

508
00:28:12,620 --> 00:28:14,580
Why so late?

509
00:28:14,620 --> 00:28:16,620
Mr. Salar, don't you know

510
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:18,780
Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama?

511
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:21,480
Mr. Salar!

512
00:28:21,980 --> 00:28:22,780
Salar!

513
00:28:22,820 --> 00:28:24,920
What a pleasure!

514
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,580
Do you know

515
00:28:26,620 --> 00:28:29,020
how many years I'm seeing you?

516
00:28:29,060 --> 00:28:33,460
The loss was all ours.

517
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:40,700
Let's drink to every mustachioed Diesel out there!

518
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:44,190
Drink your sherbet.

519
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:45,470
We have to play our part.

520
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:48,760
Listen, Mr. Dustali Khan, what I'm saying is...

521
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,985
Oh God, how we laughed!

522
00:29:00,340 --> 00:29:01,650
Where have you been?

523
00:29:01,700 --> 00:29:04,510
I went to hire a couple of musicians.

524
00:29:04,560 --> 00:29:08,300
In Abbas Khan's band there's a Black Abdollah

525
00:29:08,350 --> 00:29:12,350
who has you in stitches when he plays the blackface clown.

526
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:14,930
Asghar dear is very good company.

527
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:16,595
I'll come later.

528
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,510
No, I forget his name.

529
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:20,540
Your father's half-sister's son.

530
00:29:20,580 --> 00:29:21,440
Really?

531
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:22,380
Yes.

532
00:29:22,420 --> 00:29:25,520
You didn't come to the cafe last night. I waited after the show.

533
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:27,040
I wish you'd brought him.

534
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:29,200
He's one of those funny blackface clowns.

535
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:30,980
Of course, he's a bit of a lowlife,

536
00:29:31,020 --> 00:29:32,960
but very funny.

537
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:33,840
Pity.

538
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:35,780
Pity I couldn't find him.

539
00:29:35,820 --> 00:29:38,080
I adore blackface clowns.

540
00:29:38,120 --> 00:29:39,820
If you know where he is,

541
00:29:39,860 --> 00:29:41,580
my chauffeur will go fetch him.

542
00:29:41,620 --> 00:29:44,140
Don't you know where he can be found?

543
00:29:44,180 --> 00:29:46,560
It seems he's related to you somehow.

544
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:49,255
He's your half-sister's son, isn't he?

545
00:29:49,540 --> 00:29:50,340
Uncle Asdollah,

546
00:29:50,380 --> 00:29:52,050
they're going to fight now.

547
00:29:52,100 --> 00:29:53,260
Oh no.

548
00:29:53,740 --> 00:29:54,860
I've heard that

549
00:29:54,900 --> 00:29:56,460
the late father, God rest him,

550
00:29:56,500 --> 00:29:58,180
of Mr. Aspiran

551
00:29:59,260 --> 00:30:00,440
always wished

552
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:02,940
to see his son's wedding with his own eyes.

553
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:06,820
The Aspiran's father, God rest his soul.

554
00:30:06,870 --> 00:30:08,810
God rest him.

555
00:30:09,540 --> 00:30:11,990
One day, oh yes, yes,

556
00:30:12,040 --> 00:30:13,120
I remember one day,

557
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:15,180
near the end of his life, yes,

558
00:30:15,220 --> 00:30:18,560
he got overheated by the stove in the shop,

559
00:30:19,220 --> 00:30:21,660
came home and was taken ill.

560
00:30:21,700 --> 00:30:23,280
I was at his bedside.

561
00:30:23,320 --> 00:30:25,000
Do you know what he said?

562
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:30,980
He said, "I have only one wish in this world: before I die,

563
00:30:31,020 --> 00:30:34,040
to see the Aspiran's wedding."

564
00:30:35,248 --> 00:30:37,538
Bless you.

565
00:30:37,588 --> 00:30:39,203
But you know,

566
00:30:39,568 --> 00:30:41,940
this boy was so heartless

567
00:30:41,980 --> 00:30:44,760
that the man died of grief by his stove.

568
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:49,960
What, madam? By the stove?

569
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:53,240
What did your late husband do, God rest him?

570
00:30:54,608 --> 00:30:55,780
My husband,

571
00:30:55,820 --> 00:30:58,040
God rest him,

572
00:30:59,068 --> 00:31:00,423
my husband

573
00:31:01,687 --> 00:31:02,920
cooked sheep's heads.

574
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,055
Yes.

575
00:31:04,568 --> 00:31:05,930
And when he was young?

576
00:31:05,980 --> 00:31:07,075
Yes.

577
00:31:08,468 --> 00:31:09,600
When he was young,

578
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,920
he dug wells.

579
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,920
Mama, Mama!

580
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:14,920
What's shameful about that, dear? Honestly!

581
00:31:14,960 --> 00:31:16,960
Dustali, shut her up!

582
00:31:19,588 --> 00:31:20,920
Bless you.

583
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:23,550
I'm so sorry, you see,

584
00:31:23,708 --> 00:31:24,920
it's this Shazdeh's fault.

585
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:27,678
He gave me too much to drink.

586
00:31:27,728 --> 00:31:29,818
To tell the truth, he mixed arak and wine

587
00:31:29,868 --> 00:31:31,353
for me.

588
00:31:31,888 --> 00:31:32,920
Liar!

589
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,920
I do apologize.

590
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,960
I'm so ashamed.

591
00:31:38,008 --> 00:31:39,558
Not at all, madam.

592
00:31:39,608 --> 00:31:42,328
There's nothing shameful in your husband's trade.

593
00:31:42,788 --> 00:31:47,040
As it is said, the dearest to God are the most pious.

594
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:48,820
There's no shame in any trade.

595
00:31:48,860 --> 00:31:50,140
Right, Mr. Dustali?

596
00:31:50,180 --> 00:31:54,120
You have such humane ideas. Why won't you let your own nephew in the house?

597
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:57,120
Remember the day he came to your door asking for a little help

598
00:31:57,160 --> 00:31:58,820
and had a policeman throw him out?

599
00:31:58,860 --> 00:32:00,460
That wasn't because of his trade.

600
00:32:00,500 --> 00:32:02,760
It's because he became a blackface clown on the stage.

601
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:04,760
It's because he trampled on all decency.

602
00:32:04,800 --> 00:32:06,040
He became an addict.

603
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:08,020
He disgraced me. He became a dope fiend.

604
00:32:08,060 --> 00:32:11,140
You won't associate with such a man yourself,

605
00:32:11,180 --> 00:32:12,500
yet you blame others.

606
00:32:12,540 --> 00:32:13,920
Your reputation matters,

607
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:17,460
but not that of one of this country's finest aristocratic families, sir?

608
00:32:17,500 --> 00:32:18,640
I don't follow.

609
00:32:18,680 --> 00:32:21,000
You want to put Mr. Aspiran Ghias Abadi,

610
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:24,000
this respectable, honorable man, on a par with a dope fiend?

611
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:26,178
Isn't that man an opium addict?

612
00:32:26,228 --> 00:32:27,840
What? What happened?

613
00:32:27,890 --> 00:32:28,498
I don't get it.

614
00:32:28,548 --> 00:32:31,340
Do you know what you're saying or not?

615
00:32:31,380 --> 00:32:35,020
You and your whole tribe aren't fit to be my son's servants!

616
00:32:35,060 --> 00:32:38,980
Shut up, you bearded old witch! Go to hell!

617
00:32:39,020 --> 00:32:43,260
If one more word of this rubbish comes out of your mouth,

618
00:32:43,300 --> 00:32:47,300
I'll slap you so hard your nose will bleed!

619
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:50,580
Coward! Step outside and we'll teach you a lesson!

620
00:32:51,250 --> 00:32:53,600
Bless you.

621
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Stop him!

622
00:33:02,950 --> 00:33:04,718
Asghar, he's killed my son! Scoundrel!

623
00:33:04,768 --> 00:33:06,318
Come outside!

624
00:33:10,230 --> 00:33:12,050
Man, what are you doing?

625
00:33:12,100 --> 00:33:14,638
I said... you said something.

626
00:33:14,688 --> 00:33:15,640
Scoundrel!

627
00:33:15,690 --> 00:33:18,700
You've disgraced us!

628
00:33:18,790 --> 00:33:20,600
Asghar, my son!

629
00:33:25,748 --> 00:33:27,298
Come here.

630
00:33:38,490 --> 00:33:39,820
Oh, oh!

631
00:33:39,870 --> 00:33:40,968
Asghar! Asghar! Asghar!

632
00:33:41,008 --> 00:33:42,168
Where are you going?

633
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:47,200
Let him go! Let him go!

634
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:57,280
What's going on? There's a fight!

635
00:33:58,950 --> 00:34:00,640
What is it? What's happening?

636
00:34:00,688 --> 00:34:01,913
Nothing.

637
00:34:17,700 --> 00:34:20,050
Oh, good Lord!

638
00:34:20,130 --> 00:34:21,940
Watch out!

639
00:34:29,828 --> 00:34:31,918
He's killed Asghar!

640
00:34:31,968 --> 00:34:33,528
What's this?

641
00:34:33,728 --> 00:34:35,538
A kitchen knife.

642
00:34:39,648 --> 00:34:41,913
He had me by the throat, so I said let go!

643
00:35:28,968 --> 00:35:32,580
Dear Uncle's fear of English revenge had grown so great

644
00:35:32,620 --> 00:35:36,080
that, terrified of assassination, he had locked himself in a room,

645
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:42,000
and Mash Ghasem, like a brave sentry, kept watch outside his door at night.

646
00:35:42,848 --> 00:35:45,660
On Dear Uncle's orders, the whole garden was under watch,

647
00:35:45,700 --> 00:35:48,745
and no one was allowed to come or go at night.

648
00:36:11,660 --> 00:36:16,920
From the seizure of the railway in late summer until school opened in the fall,

649
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:19,355
I was cut off from Leili.

650
00:36:19,848 --> 00:36:23,180
My only hope of seeing Leili was the reopening of school.

651
00:36:23,220 --> 00:36:24,640
Mash Ghasem?

652
00:36:24,728 --> 00:36:25,540
Morning, lad.

653
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:26,140
Hello.

654
00:36:26,180 --> 00:36:26,980
Good morning.

655
00:36:27,020 --> 00:36:30,380
If you can get up this early, you could say a couple of prayers every day.

656
00:36:30,420 --> 00:36:33,680
When I grow up, I mean when I finish school, I'll pray for sure.

657
00:36:33,720 --> 00:36:35,960
Prayer doesn't care if you're big or small.

658
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,380
This world leads nowhere. Think about the next one.

659
00:36:39,420 --> 00:36:41,420
Mash Ghasem, Mash Ghasem,

660
00:36:41,460 --> 00:36:43,500
could you please give this note to Leili?

661
00:36:43,540 --> 00:36:45,300
Love on the brain again?

662
00:36:45,340 --> 00:36:46,720
No, no, no! No notes for us!

663
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:47,260
Why, what's wrong?

664
00:36:47,300 --> 00:36:48,420
Leave us alone, lad.

665
00:36:48,460 --> 00:36:51,700
We're not taking notes to Miss Leili anymore.

666
00:36:57,988 --> 00:36:59,960
Why, Mash Ghasem? What's wrong with it?

667
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,820
It's a sin

668
00:37:01,860 --> 00:37:04,280
to turn the head of someone's daughter of marrying age,

669
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:06,130
with nothing to come of it.

670
00:37:07,948 --> 00:37:09,400
We wanted to tell you...

671
00:37:09,440 --> 00:37:11,380
About Leili and me?

672
00:37:11,420 --> 00:37:13,278
No, no, no, nothing like that.

673
00:37:13,328 --> 00:37:16,633
Why won't you tell me? I promise I won't tell anyone.

674
00:37:17,608 --> 00:37:18,833
The truth is...

675
00:37:20,568 --> 00:37:22,480
I mean, the truth is, why should I lie?

676
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:24,300
The grave is this close!

677
00:37:26,068 --> 00:37:27,878
It was nothing at all.

678
00:37:27,948 --> 00:37:28,900
You won't tell me?

679
00:37:28,940 --> 00:37:31,360
Oh, this cursed tongue of ours!

680
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,200
You won't tell? Or take the note?

681
00:37:33,240 --> 00:37:35,200
Fine, Mash Ghasem, fine.

682
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:36,860
Lad, it's just that we...

683
00:37:36,900 --> 00:37:38,760
All right then, never mind. Fine.

684
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:42,240
Remember, lad, you swore you didn't hear it from us!

685
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:44,025
On my word of honor.

686
00:37:46,048 --> 00:37:50,048
The truth is, Miss Leili's wedding to Master Pouri is going ahead.

687
00:37:50,608 --> 00:37:55,660
What? Really? A wedding? How come?

688
00:37:55,700 --> 00:37:59,300
Seems Master Pouri's illness is getting better.

689
00:37:59,340 --> 00:38:02,620
I mean, all those medicines and doctors have done the trick.

690
00:38:02,660 --> 00:38:07,600
Lad, you've no idea how much the Colonel spent on Master Pouri's treatment.

691
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:11,220
We had a fellow townsman who, just like Master Pouri...

692
00:38:11,260 --> 00:38:14,695
Quick, tell me, please! Tell me everything you know!

693
00:38:16,628 --> 00:38:19,088
Honestly, lad, why should I lie?

694
00:38:19,548 --> 00:38:23,048
Ever since you kicked Master Pouri in the...

695
00:38:23,508 --> 00:38:27,073
seems they took out one of his honor's helpers.

696
00:38:27,368 --> 00:38:28,760
He's not been himself.

697
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:31,640
Seems the life and breath have gone out of his honor.

698
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:33,640
I know all that, Mash Ghasem.

699
00:38:33,680 --> 00:38:35,060
How do you know?

700
00:38:35,100 --> 00:38:36,240
The doctor's son.

701
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:40,280
He said every other day his father puts the electric machine on Pouri's belly.

702
00:38:42,248 --> 00:38:55,680
And we thought no one knew but us, Sir, the Colonel, the doctor, Pouri, his son, the Colonel's wife and us!

703
00:38:59,388 --> 00:39:04,620
Anyway, seems that electric current the doctor puts to Master Pouri's insides

704
00:39:04,660 --> 00:39:07,340
has done the trick. I mean, he's cured.

705
00:39:08,308 --> 00:39:10,740
But Master Pouri doesn't believe it.

706
00:39:10,780 --> 00:39:13,305
Seems he's lost his nerve.

707
00:39:14,348 --> 00:39:15,780
So now they want to test it.

708
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:18,640
Test it? How can they?

709
00:39:18,680 --> 00:39:20,000
Yes, lad.

710
00:39:20,040 --> 00:39:20,980
But how?

711
00:39:21,020 --> 00:39:23,840
They've found him a woman who...

712
00:39:28,368 --> 00:39:32,120
But what we're telling you, you must swear you didn't hear from us, lad.

713
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:36,260
I swear on Agha Jan's life, on the Holy Koran, on Leili's life!

714
00:39:37,608 --> 00:39:40,620
Anyway, now that Master Pouri's honor is fixed,

715
00:39:40,660 --> 00:39:46,020
they want to put a woman in front of him to test his, pardon me, honor.

716
00:39:47,388 --> 00:39:51,388
If he passes this test, then he'll marry Miss Leili.

717
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:59,300
Yesterday the doctor came to see the Colonel. They went in and shut the door.

718
00:40:00,508 --> 00:40:04,333
And we, just passing by, happened to overhear.

719
00:40:05,768 --> 00:40:09,340
The doctor said we should get him a temporary wife.

720
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:13,520
The Colonel said a temporary wife means trouble.

721
00:40:14,728 --> 00:40:19,840
Master Pouri himself said, either no wife at all, or you get us Miss Leili.

722
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:23,780
So what's he going to do now?

723
00:40:23,820 --> 00:40:26,360
Well, seems the Colonel himself,

724
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:28,220
without Master Pouri knowing,

725
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:30,040
talked to Miss Akhtar.

726
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:32,040
What did you say? Akhtar?

727
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:34,000
Aspiran Ghias Abadi's sister?

728
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:35,360
How can that be?

729
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:38,700
The Colonel himself made a deal with that dancing hussy

730
00:40:38,740 --> 00:40:40,520
to take a nice sum of money

731
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:43,150
and test Master Pouri.

732
00:40:43,528 --> 00:40:45,760
And that shrew didn't say no.

733
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:48,000
Does Dear Uncle know, Mash Ghasem?

734
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:50,420
Well, Sir hemmed and hawed at first,

735
00:40:50,460 --> 00:40:51,880
but in the end...

736
00:40:52,010 --> 00:40:54,920
Honestly, why should I lie? We don't know what happened.

737
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:56,760
What about the Aspiran? Does he know?

738
00:40:56,808 --> 00:41:02,148
Since Miss Qamar gave him a baby, this townsman of ours is too big for his boots.

739
00:41:02,248 --> 00:41:05,548
He's got no decency and no sense of honor.

740
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:06,498
Seen his baby?

741
00:41:06,548 --> 00:41:07,998
Like two peas in a pod.

742
00:41:08,048 --> 00:41:09,403
Like what?

743
00:41:10,530 --> 00:41:15,480
Two peas in a pod with Mr. Dustali Khan.

744
00:41:15,528 --> 00:41:19,178
And now, with tricks and schemes, he's thrown poor Mr. Dustali Khan

745
00:41:19,228 --> 00:41:22,660
out of the house, to grab Miss Qamar's estates.

746
00:41:22,700 --> 00:41:25,820
So who's supposed to test Pouri, and when?

747
00:41:26,800 --> 00:41:30,530
Honestly, why should I lie? We don't know that ourselves yet.

748
00:41:30,580 --> 00:41:33,220
Seems today or tomorrow

749
00:41:34,308 --> 00:41:38,133
the Colonel and his wife are going out,

750
00:41:38,368 --> 00:41:42,480
and they'll keep Master Pouri home from the office without him smelling a rat.

751
00:41:43,988 --> 00:41:47,800
Then this Miss Akhtar is to make up some excuse

752
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:52,260
to go to the Colonel's house and take care of Master Pouri.

753
00:41:52,300 --> 00:41:54,940
Get it, lad?

754
00:41:54,980 --> 00:41:57,700
So there's been a lot going on in this house.

755
00:41:57,928 --> 00:42:01,500
Mash Ghasem, would Pouri really let Akhtar test him?

756
00:42:01,540 --> 00:42:04,300
That hussy, pardon me, pardon me,

757
00:42:04,340 --> 00:42:07,380
if we'd given her a chance, she'd have tested even us, pardon me,

758
00:42:07,420 --> 00:42:09,520
a hundred times by now.

759
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:12,735
She just doesn't know we're not that kind.

760
00:42:13,128 --> 00:42:17,440
That day, seeing the thick-necked Turk escorting Leili to school,

761
00:42:17,480 --> 00:42:20,070
all my hopes went up in smoke.

762
00:42:20,468 --> 00:42:24,660
Uncle Colonel, who had seen through me, had convinced Dear Uncle Napoleon

763
00:42:24,700 --> 00:42:28,800
that the English might harm Leili on her way to school,

764
00:42:29,540 --> 00:42:35,940
and Dear Uncle, terrified, had asked him to hire a special escort for Leili.

765
00:42:35,980 --> 00:42:40,280
Mash Ghasem, what if we keep watch and don't let Akhtar test Pouri?

766
00:42:40,320 --> 00:42:45,220
Well, lad, some other time when we're not watching, she'll go test him.

767
00:42:46,720 --> 00:42:48,600
We need another plan.

768
00:42:48,640 --> 00:42:50,440
There is no other plan.

769
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:53,700
We have to keep watch. We mustn't let her.

770
00:42:53,740 --> 00:42:55,940
But Master Saeid, on your honor,

771
00:42:55,980 --> 00:43:00,160
besides us, Sir and the Colonel,

772
00:43:00,200 --> 00:43:03,960
and that hussy herself, nobody knows, mind!

773
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:08,580
If word gets out, Sir will put a bullet in our brain.

774
00:43:08,620 --> 00:43:11,420
Why? It has nothing to do with Dear Uncle.

775
00:43:11,460 --> 00:43:14,560
Why, if the English find out such a thing happened,

776
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:18,140
they'll disgrace Sir all over Iran.

777
00:43:18,180 --> 00:43:20,520
The things you say, Mash Ghasem!

778
00:43:20,560 --> 00:43:22,560
What do you know about the English?

779
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:26,940
We have to stand guard outside Sir's room all night for fear of their treachery.

780
00:43:26,980 --> 00:43:28,960
Don't worry, Mash Ghasem.

781
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:31,700
Just, for God's sake, if you find out when the test is,

782
00:43:31,740 --> 00:43:33,180
run and tell me right away.

783
00:43:33,220 --> 00:43:34,820
What do you take us for?

784
00:43:34,860 --> 00:43:38,860
We want this thing ruined even more than you do.

785
00:43:39,380 --> 00:43:43,010
The honor of a Ghias Abadi girl is like our own honor.

786
00:43:47,720 --> 00:43:49,880
Search all of Iran,

787
00:43:49,920 --> 00:43:53,660
you won't find a single place as honor-loving as the land of Ghias Abad.

788
00:43:53,700 --> 00:43:55,040
We had a fellow townsman...

789
00:43:55,080 --> 00:43:57,080
All right.

790
00:44:27,160 --> 00:44:28,780
Here goes!

791
00:44:56,100 --> 00:44:58,670
Until you've bought the goods, nobody can do a thing.

792
00:44:58,720 --> 00:45:00,205
Go on up.

793
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:06,440
Come on, easy.

794
00:45:31,700 --> 00:45:33,380
Go, Saeid, go!

795
00:45:39,080 --> 00:45:41,150
He's standing right here. Go!

796
00:45:45,100 --> 00:45:46,900
Here, I need to talk to you.

797
00:45:46,950 --> 00:45:48,600
I'm scared, Saeid. Run, go!

798
00:45:48,650 --> 00:45:49,650
I'll write you a letter now.

799
00:45:49,700 --> 00:45:51,040
For God's sake, look

800
00:45:51,080 --> 00:45:53,040
how they waste the goods!

801
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:55,040
Come on, sister, be fair,

802
00:45:55,080 --> 00:45:57,040
have a little decency.

803
00:45:57,080 --> 00:45:59,670
Here. Don't let anyone get hold of it.

804
00:45:59,760 --> 00:46:01,040
Saeid's coming!

805
00:46:01,080 --> 00:46:03,040
Wait, let me see!

806
00:46:03,080 --> 00:46:05,080
Wait! Don't run!

807
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:19,765
Now they plan to send Akhtar to test Pouri.

808
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:27,120
So the doctor prescribed a San Francisco to test his patient.

809
00:46:28,820 --> 00:46:30,250
What a brilliant doctor!

810
00:46:30,300 --> 00:46:34,030
I always said this Naser-ol-Hokama was a genius.

811
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:36,280
I wish I were his patient.

812
00:46:37,080 --> 00:46:41,420
But if I were his patient, I'd get my medicine from another pharmacy.

813
00:46:41,460 --> 00:46:44,245
Have you taken this medicine?

814
00:46:45,340 --> 00:46:46,370
No.

815
00:46:46,780 --> 00:46:50,030
God is my witness, if I ever laid a finger on Akhtar...

816
00:46:50,080 --> 00:46:52,950
Now you're going to start rumors about me?

817
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:55,980
You sly fox, so what are you going to do? Huh?

818
00:46:56,700 --> 00:46:57,320
I don't know.

819
00:46:57,360 --> 00:46:59,780
If Pouri passes this test,

820
00:46:59,820 --> 00:47:03,775
surely next week comes the proposal, then the wedding, and then...

821
00:47:04,120 --> 00:47:04,740
Moment!

822
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:06,280
Who says he'll pass?

823
00:47:06,320 --> 00:47:08,390
Such a dim student.

824
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:12,335
I hear this Akhtar is a good examiner.

825
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:14,100
You heard right.

826
00:47:14,140 --> 00:47:17,220
Nobody ever fails her exam.

827
00:47:18,100 --> 00:47:20,340
Damn me, if I'd had the sense,

828
00:47:20,380 --> 00:47:22,380
I'd have had her give you an exam first.

829
00:47:22,420 --> 00:47:22,940
Huh?

830
00:47:22,980 --> 00:47:24,260
Please, Uncle Asdollah,

831
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:26,540
I came so you'd think of something.

832
00:47:26,580 --> 00:47:28,460
There's nothing to think about.

833
00:47:28,500 --> 00:47:30,245
You kicked him in the...

834
00:47:30,380 --> 00:47:31,500
What did Mash Ghasem say?

835
00:47:31,540 --> 00:47:33,220
You wrecked one side of his honor.

836
00:47:33,260 --> 00:47:35,640
Now kick him again and wreck the other side too.

837
00:47:35,680 --> 00:47:39,060
Then your dear rival will become Mr. Pouri Khan the Eunuch,

838
00:47:39,100 --> 00:47:41,760
and you can rest easy till Judgment Day.

839
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:42,680
Huh?

840
00:47:42,720 --> 00:47:44,200
Joking again, Uncle Asdollah?

841
00:47:44,240 --> 00:47:45,320
Am I lying?

842
00:47:45,360 --> 00:47:46,060
No.

843
00:47:46,100 --> 00:47:48,660
Tomorrow another suitor comes, the day after another,

844
00:47:48,700 --> 00:47:50,260
and you'll have to drop school

845
00:47:50,300 --> 00:47:52,760
and kick people in their honor from morning till night.

846
00:47:52,800 --> 00:47:54,340
What kind of a job is that?

847
00:47:54,380 --> 00:47:56,440
What if I go tell Asghar Diesel?

848
00:47:56,480 --> 00:47:59,395
That thug who's Akhtar's boyfriend.

849
00:47:59,660 --> 00:48:00,885
Well, well!

850
00:48:01,260 --> 00:48:02,880
Bravo, what genius!

851
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:05,620
All that's missing is for you to bring that oaf

852
00:48:05,660 --> 00:48:08,640
and start a bloodbath over his mistress.

853
00:48:09,160 --> 00:48:09,940
Something easier:

854
00:48:09,980 --> 00:48:12,480
take Leili by the hand and bring her to the exam.

855
00:48:12,520 --> 00:48:13,860
No, Uncle Asdollah.

856
00:48:13,900 --> 00:48:15,940
If you haven't the guts, shall I take her?

857
00:48:15,980 --> 00:48:18,020
No, no, I gave my word of honor

858
00:48:18,060 --> 00:48:20,120
not to let anyone know who told me.

859
00:48:20,160 --> 00:48:22,120
Then why did you come and tell me?

860
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:24,000
I didn't tell you who told me.

861
00:48:24,040 --> 00:48:25,740
You've got some nerve!

862
00:48:25,780 --> 00:48:27,700
Shall I say who told you?

863
00:48:27,740 --> 00:48:29,900
If you know, say it.

864
00:48:30,696 --> 00:48:32,060
Shall I?

865
00:48:33,316 --> 00:48:34,620
Why should I lie?

866
00:48:34,660 --> 00:48:37,820
The grave is this close, lad!

867
00:48:37,860 --> 00:48:41,240
No, believe me, I swear Mash Ghasem hasn't the faintest idea.

868
00:48:41,280 --> 00:48:42,920
He hasn't?

869
00:48:42,960 --> 00:48:45,920
All right, all right, don't swear on the Koran.

870
00:48:45,960 --> 00:48:49,060
I think you should let the exam take place,

871
00:48:49,100 --> 00:48:53,400
then raise a ruckus so Pouri forgets all about love, and...

872
00:48:54,480 --> 00:48:58,640
spends another three or four months hooked up to Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama's machine.

873
00:48:59,200 --> 00:49:00,930
After that, God will provide.

874
00:49:00,980 --> 00:49:06,100
Maybe meanwhile the English will do Pouri in, to get back at Dear Uncle.

875
00:49:18,016 --> 00:49:20,541
Uncle Asdollah, Uncle Asdollah!

876
00:49:22,976 --> 00:49:24,721
Good idea, isn't it?

877
00:49:26,136 --> 00:49:28,386
Just make sure you don't blind him.

878
00:49:28,436 --> 00:49:32,261
Now tell me, where did you get this idea, Saeid dear?

879
00:49:32,516 --> 00:49:35,906
Pouri's trouble isn't just from the kick I gave him.

880
00:49:35,956 --> 00:49:38,506
Remember his military service in Ahvaz?

881
00:49:38,556 --> 00:49:41,456
The gunfire gave him shell shock.

882
00:49:41,496 --> 00:49:43,346
You unbalanced his lower half,

883
00:49:43,396 --> 00:49:45,226
now it's his upper half's turn.

884
00:49:45,276 --> 00:49:47,926
You plan to rid him of his lower and upper halves alike.

885
00:49:47,976 --> 00:49:49,746
But be very careful.

886
00:49:49,796 --> 00:49:54,050
This genius Pouri's offspring, for the future of the Iranian nation,

887
00:49:54,100 --> 00:49:56,060
must be preserved.

888
00:49:56,100 --> 00:50:00,100
Especially now that he works at the income tax office.

889
00:50:00,896 --> 00:50:02,926
Don't worry, I won't touch him.

890
00:50:02,976 --> 00:50:04,060
I know what to do.

891
00:50:04,100 --> 00:50:06,100
Where to?

892
00:50:06,976 --> 00:50:08,060
Be careful, Saeid.

893
00:50:08,100 --> 00:50:10,060
Don't rush in blindly.

894
00:50:10,100 --> 00:50:13,060
When that household spy tells you the date of the exam,

895
00:50:13,100 --> 00:50:15,060
let us know too.

896
00:50:15,100 --> 00:50:17,060
Moment!

897
00:50:17,100 --> 00:50:20,026
Don't you go upsetting Miss Akhtar, mind!

898
00:50:20,076 --> 00:50:21,060
I intend to ask her

899
00:50:21,100 --> 00:50:23,560
to give you an exam too.

900
00:50:23,836 --> 00:50:25,860
A big man like you should know San Francisco

901
00:50:25,900 --> 00:50:27,180
has a lovely climate.

902
00:50:27,220 --> 00:50:30,200
You need to learn its geography, my boy.

903
00:50:30,240 --> 00:50:31,320
Uncle Asdollah!

904
00:50:31,360 --> 00:50:32,240
Bye, Nanny.

905
00:50:32,280 --> 00:50:34,155
Godspeed, Nanny dear.

906
00:50:34,836 --> 00:50:36,580
I called and called. Where were you?

907
00:50:36,620 --> 00:50:38,280
The moment San Francisco came up,

908
00:50:38,320 --> 00:50:40,260
you suddenly appeared!

909
00:50:43,656 --> 00:50:45,540
But for those who have not studied,

910
00:50:45,580 --> 00:50:48,860
amassing money and wealth is more important.

911
00:50:48,900 --> 00:50:51,080
In the opinion of those who have not studied,

912
00:50:51,120 --> 00:50:54,620
they say, what use is knowledge?

913
00:50:54,660 --> 00:50:57,380
They say no matter how much we study, it is no use,

914
00:50:57,420 --> 00:50:59,780
because when we die, this knowledge ends,

915
00:50:59,820 --> 00:51:02,180
but if we have wealth, it does not perish.

916
00:51:02,220 --> 00:51:04,440
I love knowledge very much

917
00:51:04,480 --> 00:51:07,100
and pay no heed to those who love money.

918
00:51:07,140 --> 00:51:09,680
I do not ask God for money and wealth.

919
00:51:09,720 --> 00:51:11,320
Knowledge enlightens us.

920
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:14,006
In olden times, even a porter

921
00:51:14,056 --> 00:51:15,360
was called a scholar.

922
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:16,700
My belief is this:

923
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:17,620
knowledge beats any...

924
00:51:17,660 --> 00:51:18,800
What do you want?

925
00:51:18,840 --> 00:51:24,100
We're the servant of that young gentleman's uncle.

926
00:51:29,736 --> 00:51:32,220
Who do you mean? Who's the young gentleman?

927
00:51:32,260 --> 00:51:35,160
Who let you into the classroom during a lesson?

928
00:51:35,200 --> 00:51:36,240
Pardon?

929
00:51:36,280 --> 00:51:37,480
Honestly, sir, why lie?

930
00:51:37,520 --> 00:51:39,780
The grave is this close!

931
00:51:39,820 --> 00:51:42,060
We asked permission to come in first.

932
00:51:42,100 --> 00:51:44,040
You didn't say no,

933
00:51:44,080 --> 00:51:45,890
so we came in.

934
00:51:46,156 --> 00:51:48,020
We even said hello.

935
00:51:48,060 --> 00:51:49,340
Well, God bless you!

936
00:51:49,380 --> 00:51:52,100
Too much trouble to say a measly hello back?

937
00:51:58,236 --> 00:51:59,461
Quiet!

938
00:52:00,236 --> 00:52:02,086
I said, what do you want?

939
00:52:02,136 --> 00:52:03,480
The young gentleman's father

940
00:52:03,520 --> 00:52:04,980
has taken ill. They sent us

941
00:52:05,020 --> 00:52:07,285
to take the young gentleman home.

942
00:52:08,020 --> 00:52:09,980
Is your father ill?

943
00:52:10,020 --> 00:52:11,180
My father...

944
00:52:12,076 --> 00:52:12,980
Huh? Huh? Huh?

945
00:52:13,020 --> 00:52:15,980
I mean, no, my father... yes, sir, yes.

946
00:52:16,020 --> 00:52:16,980
What's wrong with him?

947
00:52:17,020 --> 00:52:20,980
Well, sir, the poor man was smoking his hookah,

948
00:52:21,020 --> 00:52:23,980
and suddenly, seems his breath got twisted up in his gut.

949
00:52:24,020 --> 00:52:27,980
He doubled over and let out a shriek

950
00:52:28,020 --> 00:52:30,020
and fell to the floor.

951
00:52:32,116 --> 00:52:34,970
Quiet! You lot, be quiet!

952
00:52:35,020 --> 00:52:37,020
Come here.

953
00:52:38,160 --> 00:52:40,160
Come to the blackboard.

954
00:52:55,880 --> 00:52:57,880
Well done. Sit down.

955
00:53:00,380 --> 00:53:02,380
Did you write your essay?

956
00:53:03,320 --> 00:53:04,120
Yes, sir.

957
00:53:04,160 --> 00:53:05,320
Read it.

958
00:53:05,616 --> 00:53:06,711
Yes, sir.

959
00:53:07,776 --> 00:53:10,496
Don't fluster him. Let him read, lad.

960
00:53:12,876 --> 00:53:14,360
I swear, we wrote the essay.

961
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:15,690
You wrote it?

962
00:53:16,396 --> 00:53:17,600
Then why not read it?

963
00:53:17,640 --> 00:53:19,486
Our father was sick.

964
00:53:19,536 --> 00:53:21,260
Wednesday, someone else's father was sick.

965
00:53:21,300 --> 00:53:22,950
Sir, may I say?

966
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:23,956
Sir, it was Alipour.

967
00:53:23,996 --> 00:53:25,486
Sir, it was Alipour.

968
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:27,696
Sir, it was Alipour.

969
00:53:28,496 --> 00:53:30,020
Forgive him, Mr. Teacher.

970
00:53:30,060 --> 00:53:33,740
His mind's elsewhere. He's upset about his father.

971
00:53:33,780 --> 00:53:35,850
He can't think straight.

972
00:53:37,416 --> 00:53:39,616
I'll make him think straight!

973
00:53:42,996 --> 00:53:45,391
I'll write it next time.

974
00:53:49,660 --> 00:53:51,286
Next time, sir. Sorry, sir.

975
00:53:51,336 --> 00:53:52,160
You hit people's kids?

976
00:53:52,200 --> 00:53:54,460
If your father keeled over, would you remember lessons?

977
00:53:54,500 --> 00:53:55,880
None of your business! Out!

978
00:53:55,920 --> 00:53:58,040
None of our business? It's very much our business!

979
00:53:58,080 --> 00:54:00,800
We need to know: are you a teacher or Shir-Ali the butcher?

980
00:54:00,840 --> 00:54:03,900
Next time bring a cleaver to class and spare your hand!

981
00:54:03,940 --> 00:54:06,340
Quiet!

982
00:54:06,696 --> 00:54:08,180
Somebody go get Kal Esmail

983
00:54:08,220 --> 00:54:09,360
to throw this man out.

984
00:54:09,400 --> 00:54:12,560
We'll go ourselves, don't you worry.

985
00:54:12,600 --> 00:54:15,940
Thank God we never went to skool to learn such things.

986
00:54:15,980 --> 00:54:19,220
God rest him, we had a fellow townsman back in Ghias Abad...

987
00:54:19,260 --> 00:54:20,745
Get out!

988
00:54:21,096 --> 00:54:21,860
Kal Esmail!

989
00:54:21,900 --> 00:54:23,500
Kal Esmail!

990
00:54:23,540 --> 00:54:24,586
Kal Esmail!

991
00:54:24,636 --> 00:54:26,450
Guys, he threw our teacher out!

992
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:28,450
Saeid, get out of here! Saeid, run!

993
00:54:28,500 --> 00:54:30,895
Saeid, get out of here! Saeid, run!

994
00:54:32,876 --> 00:54:33,766
Coast isn't clear.

995
00:54:33,816 --> 00:54:34,566
Let's go, lad.

996
00:54:34,616 --> 00:54:35,246
Where to?

997
00:54:35,296 --> 00:54:36,716
The teacher's gone!

998
00:54:41,086 --> 00:54:42,906
Hit it, Hamid, hit it!

999
00:54:46,500 --> 00:54:48,450
We saw that hussy at the bazaar arcade,

1000
00:54:48,500 --> 00:54:50,460
all dolled up from head to toe.

1001
00:54:50,500 --> 00:54:52,460
We said to ourselves, "Oh my!

1002
00:54:52,500 --> 00:54:54,460
Don't just sit there. Something's up."

1003
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:57,136
We didn't waste a second. We came straight to get you.

1004
00:54:57,186 --> 00:54:58,460
But on Sir's life,

1005
00:54:58,500 --> 00:55:00,650
on Miss Leili's life, don't get us caught.

1006
00:55:00,700 --> 00:55:04,700
I swear on your life, even if they cut me to pieces, I won't say you told me.

1007
00:55:08,466 --> 00:55:10,420
But why at noon?

1008
00:55:10,470 --> 00:55:13,186
Because the kids are at school, the house is empty,

1009
00:55:13,226 --> 00:55:15,416
and the office folks are at the office.

1010
00:55:15,466 --> 00:55:16,556
Did Pouri go to the office?

1011
00:55:16,606 --> 00:55:17,976
Now, lad, why should I lie?

1012
00:55:18,026 --> 00:55:20,256
We didn't see him go with our own eyes.

1013
00:55:20,306 --> 00:55:21,796
That's what tipped us off.

1014
00:55:21,846 --> 00:55:24,536
Don't you go kicking him again, mind.

1015
00:55:24,586 --> 00:55:27,116
Then this clan won't rest till they've spilled your blood.

1016
00:55:27,166 --> 00:55:28,556
You go and sniff around a bit.

1017
00:55:28,606 --> 00:55:32,056
See whether Akhtar's gone to Uncle Colonel's house.

1018
00:55:32,106 --> 00:55:34,016
I have to go buy some notebooks.

1019
00:55:34,066 --> 00:55:34,840
I'll be quick.

1020
00:55:34,880 --> 00:55:35,806
We're very worried.

1021
00:55:35,846 --> 00:55:36,896
Don't worry, Mash Ghasem.

1022
00:55:36,946 --> 00:55:38,936
If I see them doing something shameless,

1023
00:55:38,986 --> 00:55:41,156
I'll make a racket so they can't.

1024
00:55:41,206 --> 00:55:45,026
God bless you, lad. You're a man of honor.

1025
00:55:55,266 --> 00:55:56,436
Don't forget the key.

1026
00:55:56,486 --> 00:55:57,996
OK, wait by the door for me.

1027
00:55:58,046 --> 00:55:59,401
Hurry.

1028
00:56:00,226 --> 00:56:00,920
Mash Ghasem!

1029
00:56:00,960 --> 00:56:02,880
Yes, sir, we're here.

1030
00:56:02,920 --> 00:56:04,800
Good day, Doctor.

1031
00:56:04,840 --> 00:56:07,600
Mash Ghasem, I didn't see you in the garden today.

1032
00:56:07,640 --> 00:56:10,900
We went down to the bazaar arcade to sniff around a bit.

1033
00:56:10,940 --> 00:56:12,500
Sniff around?

1034
00:56:12,540 --> 00:56:14,040
Well, what's the news?

1035
00:56:14,080 --> 00:56:18,180
We found out the English still haven't dared go near Ghias Abad.

1036
00:56:18,220 --> 00:56:20,740
When Saeid comes home from school, give him this key.

1037
00:56:20,780 --> 00:56:22,740
Yes, Doctor. Hope all's well.

1038
00:56:22,780 --> 00:56:23,340
Hello, Shajoon.

1039
00:56:23,380 --> 00:56:23,980
Hello.

1040
00:56:24,020 --> 00:56:25,840
Why are you home so early today?

1041
00:56:25,880 --> 00:56:28,340
It's the start of term. We've no math teacher yet.

1042
00:56:28,380 --> 00:56:29,860
The vice principal sent us home.

1043
00:56:29,900 --> 00:56:30,980
Where are you going?

1044
00:56:31,020 --> 00:56:33,025
To Farrokh Lagha's house.

1045
00:56:33,986 --> 00:56:34,960
What for?

1046
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:37,580
My brother the Colonel says Farrokh Lagha is unwell.

1047
00:56:37,620 --> 00:56:38,840
We'll go see what's wrong.

1048
00:56:38,880 --> 00:56:40,400
What's wrong with her? Nothing!

1049
00:56:40,440 --> 00:56:41,720
She's buried everyone else.

1050
00:56:41,760 --> 00:56:42,780
Now it's her turn.

1051
00:56:42,820 --> 00:56:45,220
What do you all have against the poor woman?

1052
00:56:45,260 --> 00:56:46,380
Come too, if you like.

1053
00:56:46,420 --> 00:56:47,820
No, I've got lots of homework.

1054
00:56:47,860 --> 00:56:49,345
Let's go.

1055
00:56:50,006 --> 00:56:51,320
Mash Ghasem has the key.

1056
00:56:51,360 --> 00:56:51,620
OK.

1057
00:56:51,660 --> 00:56:53,560
There are grapes in the cold cellar. Help yourself.

1058
00:56:53,600 --> 00:56:57,200
OK, Shajoon. Bye.

1059
00:57:19,750 --> 00:57:21,495
Oh, man. Hey!

1060
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:22,720
Go in.

1061
00:57:22,760 --> 00:57:24,200
Everything's all set.

1062
00:57:24,240 --> 00:57:26,240
Only, the drinks are in the basement.

1063
00:57:26,280 --> 00:57:27,440
OK.

1064
00:58:08,210 --> 00:58:09,380
Mash Ghasem! Mash Ghasem!

1065
00:58:09,426 --> 00:58:10,911
Where are you going?

1066
00:58:11,866 --> 00:58:12,796
Where are you, lad?

1067
00:58:12,846 --> 00:58:14,136
Here.

1068
00:58:14,900 --> 00:58:16,570
Come. Come.

1069
00:58:21,066 --> 00:58:22,816
Lad, we came to tell you.

1070
00:58:22,866 --> 00:58:26,416
From our room, we were secretly watching the Colonel's house.

1071
00:58:26,466 --> 00:58:28,036
Suddenly that hussy showed up,

1072
00:58:28,086 --> 00:58:29,696
all dolled up,

1073
00:58:29,746 --> 00:58:30,796
wearing a chador.

1074
00:58:30,846 --> 00:58:32,996
She came into the garden. We watched her slyly.

1075
00:58:33,046 --> 00:58:36,016
We saw with our own eyes, she went toward the Colonel's house.

1076
00:58:36,066 --> 00:58:37,096
And Pouri's at home.

1077
00:58:37,146 --> 00:58:38,076
Honestly, why lie?

1078
00:58:38,126 --> 00:58:41,366
We haven't seen him leave the house with our own eyes yet.

1079
00:58:41,406 --> 00:58:43,210
Mash Ghasem, hurry to Uncle Asdollah's.

1080
00:58:43,260 --> 00:58:45,680
Get him here, so if there's trouble, he can watch out for me.

1081
00:58:45,720 --> 00:58:46,520
Go!

1082
00:58:46,560 --> 00:58:48,296
Yes, lad.

1083
00:58:48,346 --> 00:58:49,400
Be very careful.

1084
00:58:49,440 --> 00:58:51,120
Don't let the Colonel find out, mind.

1085
00:58:51,160 --> 00:58:53,680
If he does, your blood's on your own head.

1086
00:58:53,726 --> 00:58:54,436
OK.

1087
00:58:54,486 --> 00:58:56,360
Mash Ghasem, don't let anyone find out.

1088
00:58:56,400 --> 00:58:58,145
Yes, lad.

